@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] ci-affected-workflow
ci.yml MUST run on every trunk push and on dispatch, one run per ref and event, with a
newer push replacing a pending run. It selects with tools/affected from the
head of the newest earlier started, non-cancelled push run (so replaced pushes stay
covered), or everything when there is no usable base, and MUST run the
affected builds, tests and machine tests, evaluate every selected machine
test's assembly (`[drv]`, deferred ones included), run each machine test as its own
job wrapped in `cachix watch-exec`, and each affected Mix suite (`expensive`) as its own job
building every shard, and tools/precommit over the same range.
A push run MUST also reselect every target whose job failed in a trunk run
since the last green one (contract ci-reselect-failed). Known Inception failures, and the full
machine-test set when everything or more than 40 suites are selected (unless dispatched with
machine_all), run only in the daily backstop. A selection error, or any failed job, MUST fail the ci job
(ADR-0270).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] machine-tests-daily-backstop
nixos-machine-tests.yml MUST run every nixos_machine_test target daily, and
on dispatch the space-separated check names given in `checks`, each through
`tools/buck2 test` in its own job (ADR-0270).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] mix-nightly-fresh-seeds
mix-nightly-seeds.yml MUST run daily and on dispatch, building every Mix suite
that ci.yml's mix job can select with one `-c mix.test_salt` per run:
`nightly-<UTC date>` by default, or the dispatched salt for a replay. It MUST
print the salt, so a failure can be reproduced (contract
mix-test-seeds-explicit, ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;build] ci-namespace-cache
ci.yml's affected, build, hosts, test, evaluate, machine and precommit jobs,
nixos-machine-tests.yml's jobs and oss-scanner.yml's image job MUST receive the Namespace token only as the
job environment variable NAMESPACE_RBE_TOKEN from the repository secret, never
in argv, a file in the checkout or a log, so tools/buck2 enables the Namespace
cache. A run without the secret (a fork or pull request) MUST still build
locally through the same steps (ADR-0276).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;release] mila-release-publish-tag-only
mila-release.yml MUST create a GitHub release, or upload to any store, only in
a run for a pushed `refs/tags/mila-v*` tag (`github.event_name == 'push'`): the
publish job and its tag-only needs (source-bundle, linux, windows) carry that
explicit `if:`. A run on any other trigger (workflow_dispatch on any ref, a
trunk push) MUST NOT publish and MUST NOT enter the `mila-release`
environment or read a signing secret; its android and apple jobs build
unsigned (`unsigned-*` artifacts, 7-day retention). A tag run MUST refuse a
missing signing input rather than publish an unsigned artifact (ADR-0235).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;release] mila-release-signing-leak
mila-release.yml's android and apple jobs MUST run with
OVERALLS_BUCK2_REMOTE=off and, in signed runs, MUST fail when a signing value
(the Apple keychain and certificate passwords, notary key id and issuer, the
decoded ExportOptions.plist, the Android upload passwords, keystore path or
keystore bytes) reaches a Buck2 log, buck-out, the daemon's files or a buck2
temporary directory, or the Apple identity reaches an action command or
environment. Signing material MUST live only in owner-only $RUNNER_TEMP files
removed by an always() step, and passwords MUST NOT appear in argv
(ADR-0235, ADR-0269 M9).
